WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
For six years, a man called Siddhattha
Gotama fasted almost to death,

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.500
searching for the truth.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.610
It brought him no insight.

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.840
So he ate again, sat under a
tree, and turned his mind inward.

5
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.970
Buddhists say that by the end of that
night he had woken up to things as they

6
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.470
really are.

7
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.770
He was called the
Buddha: the awakened one.

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.060
But can sitting still and looking inward
really show you the truth about reality?

9
00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:32.080
In this mission, you'll follow
that night of awakening,

10
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.720
and compare two great Buddhist traditions,

11
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.000
Theravada and Mahayana.

12
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.160
Then you'll hear what critics
say about such experiences,

13
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.020
and weigh up the replies.

14
00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.450
Your mission: weigh up whether looking
inward can show you what is real.
